    "Id": "vehiclechassisdef_gerrida_GDR-D",
    "Name": "Gerrida",
    "Details": "The D configuration of the Gerrida hovertank was derived from the second prototype batch and pairs seven jump jets with six SRM-4 launchers, a Medium Pulse Laser and a Light TAG in its turret. Getting close enough to use SRMs is very risky for a hovertank, but its jump capability and heavy armor make it highly likely to reach the best striking distance. Like every Gerrida, it is reserved for elite Society vehicle crews.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 7/11 hexes / 210/330 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Ferro-Lamellor (C)\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       225     70\n<b>Left</b>         180     70\n<b>Right</b>       180     70\n<b>Rear</b>        150     70\n<b>Turret</b>      200     70\n\n<b>Total</b>      935    350</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Distracting</color>\n\n<color=#ffcc00> Omni Vehicle</color>",
    "Icon": "Gerrida"
  },
  "YangsThoughts": "Seven jump jets on a super-heavy hovertank? Now I’ve seen everything. With a 210-meter jump it can practically drop those six SRM-4s right on top of somebody, and it’s got enough armor to survive getting there. Just try not to think too hard about what happens when all that tonnage comes back down.",
